==English==

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|en-us-morbid.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Etymology===
from {{etyl|la}} [[morbidus]] "diseased", from [[morbus]] "sickness", itself from the root of [[mori]] "to die" or directly from the Proto-Indo-European base *mor- "to rub, pound, wear away"

===Adjective===
{{en-adjective}}

# {{originally}} of, or relating to [[disease]]
# [[unhealthy]] or [[unwholesome]], especially [[psychologically]]: mentally [[sick]]([[sickly|ly]])
# suggesting the [[horror]] of [[death]]; [[macabre]] or [[ghoulish]]
# [[grisly]] or [[gruesome]]

====Derived terms====
* [[morbidity]]
* [[morbidly]]
* [[morbidness]]

====Related terms====
* [[morbidezza]]
* [[morbilous]]

====Synonyms====
*(''of or relating to disease''): [[pathological]]
*(''unhealthy or unwholesome, especially psychologically''): [[sick]], [[twisted]], [[unhealthy]], [[unwholesome]], [[warped]]
*(''suggesting the horror of death''): [[black]], [[ghoulish]], [[grim]], [[macabre]]
*(''grisly, gruesome''): [[bloody]], [[disgusting]], [[gory]], [[grisly]], [[gruesome]], [[sickening]]

